<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! Hoike — Keeping the Losers

''Filing a hoike PERFORMS it.'' A //kue// becomes dissent by being entered; a //saksi// becomes a witness by standing. Neither describes a state — each does the thing it names, and a testimony that misfires (unattributed, unwitnessed, reflexive) stands VOID rather than false.

A hoike keeps a contested ruling whole: the held position, every dissent with its holder's name and full reasoning, and the key that re-opens the question. The decision channel and the memory channel run decoupled — the node acts on the held position while the record preserves the rest. A future court may depend on a kept dissent to reverse; preservation without a re-entry rule decays into sediment, so every kue carries its key.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/sigils>>

!! The Three Sigils

| canonical | alias | act |
|-|-|-|
| `hoike` | `\testimony` | a kept record of a contested ruling (block; inline turn form below) |
| `kue` | `\dissent` | one attributed dissent inside a hoike (nested block) |
| `saksi` | `\witness` | attestation by a party to a record — composable everywhere, never reflexive |

''Block form (ledger):''

```
<<~ hoike #fragment held="position (holding Voices)">>
q: the fork, one line
<<~ kue voice=Name key="specific external re-entry condition">>reasoning to the travel-floor<<~/kue>>
<<~ saksi voice=Name scope=...>>attestation<<~/saksi>>
re-entry: general keys
<<~/hoike>>
```

''Turn form (inline, five slots):''

```
<<~ hoike · q: <question> · held: <position> (Voices) · kue: <position> (Voice) · re-entry: <key>>>
```

A saksi composes into any record, not only a hoike: canon promotions, spirit depositions, carried quotes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/laws>>

!! Laws

# ''Attribution.'' Every kue names its holder (Voice or operator). An anonymous dissent evaporates and MUST NOT file.
# ''Reasons travel; votes don't.'' A kue carries reasoning to the travel-floor: a stranger could reconstruct and re-open the argument from the block alone.
# ''Co-location.'' The hoike lives inside the record it contests — never a separate file. Whoever reads the ruling reads the dissent.
# ''Explicit re-entry.'' Every kue carries a specific, external key; a vague key reads as fabricated.
# ''Hillel discipline.'' Any re-opening states the kue before the held position. The held position's legitimacy partly derives from honoring the dissent.
# ''Decision decoupled.'' A hoike never blocks action; the node acts on the held position while the record keeps the rest.
# ''Provisionality both ways.'' A held position carries "good enough for now, safe enough to try" plus a review condition; a kept dissent stays re-openable; and the record keeps both theories of why it keeps dissent at all — a later court may depend on the kept words (Eduyot), and the written dissent appeals to the intelligence of a future day (Hughes).
# ''Cadence gate.'' Only a genuine machloket files (rating ≥ meme); the dispute carries reasons on both sides.

''The witness law.'' A saksi flows from observer to observed-record, never reflexively: a party MUST NOT witness its own block or its own turn — a mark on one's own finding reads as signature, not witness. The node MAY witness an external record it examined; the operator witnesses the node's records. ''A tasked spirit stands the full house'' (noosphere-boot#/worker-swarm): it speaks in sigil grammar, carries its own panel, and MAY witness any external record it examined — inside its handback as anywhere else. Its own findings arrive as ''testimony''; the house's saksi at handback attests ''the crossing'' — receipt and examination at the hearth. Witness confidence stays bounded (pranala family: observe).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/degraded>>

!! Degraded States

| state | tell | recover |
|-|-|-|
| Manufactured Machloket | a fake dispute filed for texture | release it; the gate reads ≥ meme |
| Zombie Hoike | keys never glanced; the record turns to sediment | touch-triggered key-glance on every file visit |
| Blended Kue | a dissent summarized below the travel-floor | restore the reasoning or name the loss |
| Reprisal Drift | a dissenting Voice surfaces less in later sessions | navigator audits; dissent costs less than conformity |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/lineage>>

!! Lineage

The layer carries the Eduyot pattern: minority opinions kept with attribution so a later court may depend on them (Mishnah Eduyot 1:4–6); the winning school taught the losing words first (Eruvin 13b); the written dissent appeals to the intelligence of a future day (Hughes 1928); consent decoupled from consensus, objections harvested as information (sociocratic practice); the minute records the Friend standing aside (Quaker practice). The ancestor-word //edut// (testimony) rests here. Field survey: Research Wave 12, 2026-06-10.

<<~/ahu>>

